      "created_at": "2024-09-11T03:24:23.944Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hello everyone,</p>\n<p>Is ERPNext not compatible with many transactions or big data?</p>\n<p>I have a pretty serious problem. The transactions that occurred formed a very large “Repost Item Valuation” So that my report (Balance Sheet or Stock Balance) did not display the correct data.</p>\n<p>Do you have a solution to this problem?<br>\n.<br>\nIn addition, I use a fairly capable server (Digitalocean)<br>\nCPU: 32 Core<br>\nRAM: 64 GB<br>\n.<br>\n<div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/7/1/71abd7041490379ce0771ba0d14b60525bad7055.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/71abd7041490379ce0771ba0d14b60525bad7055\" title=\"Repost-Item-Valuation\"><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/7/1/71abd7041490379ce0771ba0d14b60525bad7055_2_690x435.jpeg\" alt=\"Repost-Item-Valuation\" data-base62-sha1=\"gdA7pcZWNu6290dknJVQ82ezned\" width=\"690\" height=\"435\" srcset=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/7/1/71abd7041490379ce0771ba0d14b60525bad7055_2_690x435.jpeg, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/7/1/71abd7041490379ce0771ba0d14b60525bad7055_2_1035x652.jpeg 1.5x, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/7/1/71abd7041490379ce0771ba0d14b60525bad7055.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"F7F8F9\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">Repost-Item-Valuation</span><span class=\"informations\">1316×831 143 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>",
